          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "To automate order entry, shop-floor data capture, and operational workflows **without ripping and replacing your ERP**, you need a consultant skilled in **\"wrapper\" architectures**. In this model, Microsoft Power Platform and Azure Integration Services sit on top of your existing database or APIs to deliver modern mobile apps and automated pipelines.\n\nThe consulting landscape in Perth ranges from industrial-scale Microsoft partners to nimble local boutiques:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Enterprise & Industrial WA Specialists (Best for complex/large-scale operations)\n\n*   **Velrada (an NRI Company)**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Headquartered in Perth (St Georges Terrace), one of Australia’s most decorated Microsoft Business Applications partners.\n    *   **Why them:** Deep experience across WA’s industrial, mining, and discrete manufacturing sectors. They specialize in enterprise Power Platform deployments that orchestrate legacy back-ends (like SAP, Pronto, Epicor, or Syspro) without replacing the underlying system of record.\n*   **Insight (formerly Ignia)**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Significant local engineering and digital innovation team based in the Perth CBD.\n    *   **Why them:** Ignia was born in Perth and established a reputation for building robust custom connectors, cloud integrations, and mobile solutions for field and industrial workers. They are well-suited if your shop floor requires custom edge integration, offline data caching, or hardware/scanner integration.\n*   **Data#3**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Longstanding presence on Adelaide Terrace.\n    *   **Why them:** One of Microsoft’s largest Australian systems integrators. They have dedicated practices for Business Applications and automation (both cloud Power Automate and Power Automate Desktop RPA), ideal if your legacy ERP lacks modern APIs and requires screen-scraping/robotic entry.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Manufacturing & ERP Integration Specialists (Best for mid-market)\n\n*   **Professional Advantage**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Dedicated Perth team.\n    *   **Why them:** Unlike pure low-code agencies, Professional Advantage specializes in mid-market manufacturing and warehousing. They understand production scheduling, BOMs, inventory flow, and lot tracking, making them adept at designing shop-floor capture apps that feed cleanly into back-office financials.\n*   **Barhead Solutions**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** National Microsoft partner with strong WA project delivery.\n    *   **Why them:** Barhead is among Australia's foremost Power Platform and AI specialists. They excel at implementing **AI Builder and Azure Document Intelligence** for order processing (e.g., turning incoming customer purchase orders in PDF/email format directly into structured ERP orders with human-in-the-loop validation).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Local Perth Boutiques (Best for rapid pilots and agile delivery)\n\n*   **Opticloud Solutions**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Local boutique on St Georges Terrace.\n    *   **Why them:** Focused specifically on Power Platform, Power Automate, and custom app delivery for WA businesses. Ideal if you want to run a rapid, cost-effective proof-of-concept (POC) for a specific production cell or automated order queue without large enterprise overhead.\n*   **Eversdale Technology**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** Local Perth specialists in Power Platform and Dynamics.\n    *   **Why them:** Long-running local team with practical experience extending existing business systems through custom low-code tools.\n*   **Lateral**\n    *   **Perth Footprint:** East Perth-based custom software and systems integration consultancy.\n    *   **Why them:** If your ERP is an older on-premise system or proprietary database where standard Microsoft connectors do not work out of the box, Lateral specializes in bridging legacy databases with modern cloud apps and APIs.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look For and Questions to Ask\n\nWhen briefing these consultants, your non-replacement constraint changes the requirements:\n\n1. **ERP Connector Strategy:** Ask, *\"How will the Power Platform talk to our specific ERP (e.g., REST API, staging database, Azure Logic Apps, or Power Automate Desktop RPA)?\"* Avoid any vendor who suggests custom-coding everything from scratch if a lightweight middleware pipeline will do.\n2. **Shop-Floor User Experience & Hardware:** A tablet app on a clean desk behaves differently than one on a dusty production floor. Ask how they design for **ruggedized tablets/scanners (e.g., Zebra devices), barcode/QR input**, and whether the apps have **offline caching** if your factory has Wi-Fi dead zones.\n3. **Licensing Optimization:** Power Platform licensing can escalate quickly if every shift worker requires a full Power Apps premium license. An experienced partner will structure your architecture (e.g., shift-based pooled kiosks, Power Pages, or Dataverse-multiplexing compliant models) to keep software costs under control.\n4. **Order Automation / OCR Experience:** Ask to see live examples of how they handle multi-line order processing from customer PO PDFs (using Microsoft AI Builder / Power Automate) and how exceptions are routed for human review before touching the ERP.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
